1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY & MODEL SPECIFICATIONS
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This report captures the complete empirical evaluation of the Telemetry Trust Score models
designed to safeguard Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA) against telemetry corruptions.

Models Evaluated:
  [1] Existing Baseline Model (Linear Weighted Sum):
      Formula: T_s = 0.40 * S_fresh + 0.30 * S_cont + 0.30 * S_valid
      Core Flaw: Subject to additive compensation masking; memoryless (zero uncertainty estimation).

  [2] Distinct NAB-Trust Model (Non-Linear Adaptive Bayesian-Entropy Model):
      Formula: T_s = Gate(S_min) * [ 0.85 * (mu_bayes - z * sigma_unc) + 0.15 * S_cohere ]
      Innovations: Anti-compensation T-norm gating, dynamic Shannon entropy weights,
                   Beta-prior recursive Bayesian state estimation, and multivariate semantic coherence.

